 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Take the old seat and handlebars to a shop. They can measure the height from the upper part of your seat tube, not the bar tops. No problem. Your new seat should sit about the same height off the ground, so you' not too high or too low. Then you could try a slightly longer stem, or swap the seat tube down a little in the frame. Short stems and high seats can strain your back. Probably, but the bike feels longer and lower, which some people like. You can add a little spacer under the stem if it feels too long.",
